# PREDICTION for the next ROOT lane run (run 14), committed ALONE and BEFORE the run.
#
# STEP -1 of `scratch/lane-run-7-procedure.md`. The derivation is written out so it is
# checkable independently of whether the number turns out to match — R19-06 and R20-07 are the
# two runs whose FIGURE was right and whose EXPLANATION was reconstructed afterwards, which is
# the failure this file exists to prevent.
#
# ORDERING IS CONVENTION, NOT MECHANISM (D0A-R22-01, reopened). `git log` on this file versus
# the result file is the only evidence that the prediction came first. It held for run 13.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY RUN 14 IS OWED: D0A-R24-01 IS REOPENED.
#
# Run 13 was recorded as the full-hygiene run closing R24-01. D0A-R25-05 withdrew one of its
# checks: the procedure claimed "an unchanged set of hashes after a forced rebuild is the
# proof" while its commands computed NO hashes — `| tail -3` printed three artifact PATHS (and
# masked cargo's exit status, having no pipefail), and the forced rebuild went to /dev/null.
# So run 13's counts carry an unproven premise: that the binaries executed were built from the
# tree being measured. That cannot be repaired after the fact. Run 14 re-establishes it under
# the corrected section 2b, which hashes the FULL enumerated set before and after a forced
# rebuild and refuses a short list.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DERIVATION
#
# Base: run 13 measured EXECUTED 177 / SKIPPED 5 / reported 182 at root.
#       The current unprivileged pair is EXECUTED 167 / SKIPPED 25 / reported 192 (measured
#       2026-09-06 at 3b9ce08, and independently re-measured by the pre-commit hook at both
#       3b9ce08 and e4a8f05 across all 17 targets).
#
# Delta since run 13: the round-25 remediation added TEN tests and removed none.
# Each was checked for root-gating BY GREP of its body — a geteuid check, a SKIP branch, a
# bwrap_available guard — not from memory:
#
#   canonicalize.rs  an_empty_argv_is_refused_during_canonicalization            no gate
#   canonicalize.rs  a_fifo_executable_is_refused_promptly_...                   no gate
#   canonicalize.rs  a_character_device_executable_is_refused_on_type            no gate
#   canonicalize.rs  an_oversized_executable_is_refused_on_size                  no gate
#   canonicalize.rs  a_real_large_executable_is_still_accepted                   SKIP branch *
#   execute.rs       a_directly_built_action_with_an_empty_argv_..._at_execute   no gate
#   service.rs       a_tier_the_daemon_cannot_enforce_is_denied_...              no gate
#   service.rs       the_enforced_tier_passes_the_tier_check_and_reaches_gate    no gate
#   service.rs       an_elapsed_consent_window_..._wall_clock_is_frozen_...      no gate
#   service.rs       a_granted_entry_without_a_monotonic_instant_...             no gate
#
#   * The one SKIP branch gates on a PATH EXISTING, not on euid:
#     `/usr/bin/coreutils` (root:root 0755, 11352352 bytes on this box). Root sees the same
#     file, so it EXECUTES in both environments. This is the only one of the ten whose
#     outcome could differ between lanes, and it does not.
#
# CORRECTED POST-HOC (D0A-R26-06). The paragraph that stood here said all four service tests
# "use a socketpair and a stub SessionSource, reach a denial BEFORE any gate, PAM call or
# spawn". **The number it supported was right and the explanation was wrong** — the R19-06 /
# R20-07 shape, third occurrence, and this time inside the file whose whole purpose is that the
# derivation be checkable independently of whether the number matches. What is actually true:
#
#   a_tier_the_daemon_cannot_enforce_…    socketpair + Seatless, via serve_one_action;
#                                         denies at the TIER check, before the store
#   the_enforced_tier_passes_…            socketpair + Seatless, via serve_one_action;
#                                         passes the tier check, is STORED, then denies AT THE
#                                         GATE — which is the point of it, and the opposite of
#                                         "before any gate"
#   an_elapsed_consent_window_…           NO socketpair, NO Seatless; calls
#                                         present_and_execute directly
#   a_granted_entry_without_…             NO socketpair, NO Seatless; calls
#                                         present_and_execute directly
#
# The CONCLUSION survives — none of the four needs a privileged facility, so all four execute
# at root — but it survives for two different reasons, not one. This annotation is added after
# the run rather than rewritten silently: the file's protected property (prediction before
# measurement) rests on commit order (af6dde0 precedes 53e2b5a), not on its wording, so a
# labelled correction costs nothing and hiding the error would cost the record.
#
# So all ten execute at root:  177 + 10 = 187 EXECUTED.
# None of them skips in either lane, so the root skip set is UNCHANGED at 5:
#   b1_daemon_binary                      needs --features insecure-test-seams
#   an_unreadable_login_defs              this uid can read a 0000 file          (root-caused)
#   a_regular_login_user_is_not_refused   running as root                        (root-caused)
#   pidfd_refuses_a_recycled_pid_barrier  userns unavailable to root here        (root-caused)
#   live_logind_query                     standing DEFER
#
# CONSISTENCY CHECK, because the two lanes must describe the SAME test set:
#   unprivileged  167 + 25 = 192 reported
#   root          187 +  5 = 192 reported
# A run 14 whose `reported` is not 192 means the test SET changed, not the skip distribution —
# a different defect from a count mismatch, and it must be diagnosed as such.
#
# Root and unprivileged remain OVERLAPPING SETS, neither a superset: three of the five root
# skips execute unprivileged. 187 > 167 is NOT a coverage claim and must not be read as one.
#
# A MISMATCH IS A RESULT. Record which side was wrong. Do not adjust this derivation until it
# agrees with the measurement.

EXPECTED_EXECUTED=187
EXPECTED_SKIPPED=5
EXPECTED_REPORTED=192
